ANTEATER POKER
==============

Anteater Poker is an online Texas Hold'em variant for Linux. A server hosts
the table and players connect as clients. The game includes the Anteater card:
in a player's hand it acts as a wildcard, while on the board it replaces the
community cards and advances the game to the final round.

BUILD
-----

Run:

    make

The compiled programs are:

    bin/poker_server
    bin/poker_client

The graphical client requires GTK+ 3 and Fontconfig development packages.

RUNNING A GAME
--------------

Start the server in one terminal:

    make run-server

Start each client in another terminal:

    make run-client

The default host and port are configured in the Makefile. To override them:

    make run-server PORT=10215
    make run-client HOST=localhost PORT=10215

The server must be reachable from each client machine. The first player can
start the game after players join; remaining seats are filled by bots.

When using the precompiled customer package, start the programs directly:

    ./bin/poker_server 10215
    ./bin/poker_client localhost 10215

More information about the game rules is in Poker_UserManual.pdf. The source
archive places this manual at doc/Poker_UserManual.pdf.

TESTING
-------

Run the communication smoke test:

    make test_comm

The following targets build and launch each application for interactive
testing:

    make test_server
    make test_client

Create the compressed source package:

    make tar

This generates Poker_Beta_src.tar.gz.

Create the customer package:

    make customer_tar

This generates Poker_Beta.tar.gz with the documentation, resources, compiled
server, and graphical client executable.

CLEANUP
-------

Remove generated executables with:

    make clean
